Carafe bench: the area a core read last needs no new check while the GPU has modified nothing since, so CPU reads
inside it skip OnCPURead again. Every place that marks guest memory as GPU-modified advances an epoch, and an area
checked at another epoch is checked again; a cache invalidation by the program always checks. 0012 dropped the area
altogether, and every small CPU read of GPU-tracked memory took two locks and walked the caches.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

